The MZ topology overcomes several challenges associated with optomechanical amplification, such as pump noise rejection (see~\Cref{sec:RIN}). One further advantage of the MZ configuration is that the pump and signal exit at separate ports. The signal can then be read out (e.g. using homodyne detection) without the strong amplifier pump field saturating the detection photodiodes.

